# ISDB-T (1seg) tuner node for the docomo GALAXY S III (SC-06D).
#
# drivers/media/nmi326 registers a character device (major 225, minor 0) and
# then calls class_create()/device_create(), so ueventd creates /dev/isdbt on
# its own. What ueventd does NOT know is who should own it: without a rule it
# lands as root:root 0600 and nothing in the framework can open it.
#
# The clean fix is a ueventd rule. d2att-unified installs ueventd.qcom.rc to
# the root of the ramdisk, so the line
#
#     /dev/isdbt   0660   media   media
#
# belongs in a d2dcm fork of that file. This .rc is the low-risk alternative:
# it does the same thing from init, works no matter which ueventd file is
# actually installed, and is easy to drop once the ueventd route is in place.
#
# Imported from init.qcom.rc? No - nothing imports this file yet.
# TODO(hardware): add `import /init.oneseg.rc` to the d2dcm ramdisk, or fold
# these commands into the ueventd rule above. Until then this file is
# installed but inert, which is deliberate: an unreferenced .rc cannot break
# a boot, and boot comes first.

on post-fs
    # The driver is built in (CONFIG_ISDBT_NMI=y), so it has probed long
    # before post-fs and /dev/isdbt already exists. chown/chmod on a missing
    # path is logged and ignored, so this is safe on a unit without a tuner.
    chown media media /dev/isdbt
    chmod 0660 /dev/isdbt

    # Group ownership choice: `media` is what the framework's media stack runs
    # as, and a 1seg app streams TS into the media pipeline. If the stock
    # stack turns out to run its own uid, change both lines to match it - the
    # value has to agree with whatever sepolicy/isdbt.te allows.
